{
  "about": "Which KvKs the Council can save: checkKvk in site/kingdom.js (the admin page's check before Save) and save_kvk in supabase/migrations must refuse the same ones with the same sentence. tests/kvk.test.js and supabase/tests/test_kvk.py run every case; the SQL test clears the saved KvKs inside its rolled-back transaction and saves `others` first. An `id` names one of `others`: the KvK being edited. A new KvK (no `id`) names its Story by slug (site/kvk-stories.js); `others` are saved KvKs, some from before Stories, so the SQL test writes them straight into the table. Periods are Counting Periods, numbered from 1 in the order given.",
